{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a89ac1e3c50a9d6c4303c919a4a4e1380d01cfb16b740343b4f57bd747775c38","digest":{"component_or_area":"type checking / mypy ratchet","key_entities":["pyproject.toml","disallow_untyped_defs","disallow_any_explicit","tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py","docs/architecture.md","rebar._cli","rebar._snapshot","rebar._store","rebar.reducer","rebar.schemas","rebar.audit","rebar._io","rebar._engine_support","rebar.opcert_service","rebar.review_bot","rebar.grounding","rebar.graph","rebar.attest","rebar.metrics"],"problem_keywords":["type annotations","mypy strictness","ratchet enforcement","loose typing","explicit Any"],"propositions":["Repo-wide type coverage is incomplete; 12 packages have untyped function definitions and explicit Any usages that are not enforced by the mypy ratchet","The mypy ratchet currently only constrains disallow_untyped_defs but allows Any to pass validation, creating a loophole for loose typing in signed code","37 untyped defs across 12 packages can be remediated with straightforward annotations (return types and parameter type hints) without introducing new Any","Establishing a two-tier ratchet (tier 1: disallow_untyped_defs; tier 2: disallow_any_explicit) would prevent regression of explicit Any usage in typed packages","The test harness and documentation must be updated to track and enforce both ratchet tiers as shrink-only constraints"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787314653933554001,"uuid":"01ef6075-02f8-4025-8ce0-400e46445cf4"}